    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33377" root="فرج" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْجَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَجٌ</span>, in five places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  It is said in
the T, that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْرَكُوا القَوْمَ عَلَى فَرْجَتِهِمْ</span> or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرْجَتِهِمْ</span></b> 
occurs in a trad. as meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">على هزِيمَتِهِمْ</span> [i. e.
<i>They overtook the people,</i> or <i>party, in their state
of defeat</i>]: but it is also related as with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قاف</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حآء</span> [app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْحَتِهِمْ</span>]. (TA.)

